                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4bf5fb22-0dc3-3a22-a43c-a5ae0883b56c",
                        "entry_id": "169f79a8-74cd-30de-b694-d08f5f8b2e5a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Hautbois renaissance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "note": "Le terme historique est « hautbois », c’est le seul qui figure dans les traités d’époque ; le terme « chalemie » a été introduit lors du regain d’intérêt pour les instruments anciens au xxᵉ siècle, pour éviter la confusion avec le hautbois moderne",
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "15151518-2442-4883-ac58-119800597eed",
                                "sense_id": "4bf5fb22-0dc3-3a22-a43c-a5ae0883b56c",
                                "text": "D’où l’attachement de Rohmer au réalisme des instruments utilisés (le luth, la chalemie, la flûte traversière), à la pertinence historique des partitions reprises, à l’élégance des choristes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9601ac52-ca2b-4297-a90c-ac2ada9382fb",
                        "source_entry_id": "169f79a8-74cd-30de-b694-d08f5f8b2e5a",
                        "source_sense_id": "4bf5fb22-0dc3-3a22-a43c-a5ae0883b56c",
                        "target_lang_word": "shawm",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shawm",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5de3ffa9-0d15-3346-b0e1-57b3d1c83c5b",
                                        "entry_id": "543e848a-4147-3ff0-baaa-9416f112a88a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mediaeval double-reed wind instrument with a conical wooden body."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa7e9375-a4f1-438c-a2b9-cce890414c71",
                                                "sense_id": "5de3ffa9-0d15-3346-b0e1-57b3d1c83c5b",
                                                "text": "And all the field is thick with companies\nOf fair-clothed men that play on shawms and lutes\nAnd gather honey of the yellow fruits\nBetween the branches waxen soft and wide"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5d660a2-c8cb-46a2-a099-f03a34d46cb2",
                                                "sense_id": "5de3ffa9-0d15-3346-b0e1-57b3d1c83c5b",
                                                "text": "There are four flutes, a harp of twenty strings, a mournful shawm, and a number of drums of oxhide, some to be struck, others spanked."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "52f5e5b8-8cd9-4017-8131-226ab9d88f17",
                        "source_entry_id": "169f79a8-74cd-30de-b694-d08f5f8b2e5a",
                        "source_sense_id": "4bf5fb22-0dc3-3a22-a43c-a5ae0883b56c",
                        "target_lang_word": "shalm",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shalm",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5a7c30b-73ca-3a99-a711-ff07051cdfa9",
                                        "entry_id": "561ba954-2b5f-3782-9804-e93acf5b1e74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Obsolete form of shawm."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec97b5de-181e-4c75-bd5e-ad975728a8d9",
                                                "sense_id": "b5a7c30b-73ca-3a99-a711-ff07051cdfa9",
                                                "text": "These few words were continually repeated, and to describe the sound, it was as if you heard forest-horns and shalms sounded together from a far distance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc2567fb-34e6-40ba-917d-57dffd7d0d8c",
                                                "sense_id": "b5a7c30b-73ca-3a99-a711-ff07051cdfa9",
                                                "text": "Paris flings up her windows, claps hands, as the Avengers, with their shrilling drums and shalms tramp by...."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
